# tally 2.3.1 R1, N250.8 (E §4.2 step 3: a hole-day decision doesn't run, "a read of its legs is that hole";
# C-13.9): the hole both ways, by name (d_to) and through a binding's `where` on its place (b_konto: pw's place
# is the hole, so its where is); a plan's leg place needs no day. Before: b_konto 0, pw's place read as konto's
# other.
=== holeday_b.tally
model holeday
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place save: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input lim: money PLN
input hd: date

move pw: transfers
  reads konto
  on hd
  leg cash from konto to other amount amt + 0 * bal(konto)

move px: transfers
  reads konto
  on hd
  leg cash from konto to save amount min(amt, bal(konto))

move plan: transfers
  on hd
  leg cash from save to other amount amt


version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[save] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[other] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  lim = 50.00 PLN "s"
  hd = ?"which day?" "s"
ask b_save: count(m in transfers over 2026 where m.cash.to == save)
ask b_other: count(m in transfers over 2026 where m.cash.to == other)
ask d_to: pw.cash.to
ask b_konto: count(m in transfers over 2026 where m.cash.to == konto)
=== expect
b_konto: ?"which day?" (hd)
  cut 2026-04-20
b_other: ?"which day?" (hd)
  cut 2026-04-20
b_save: ?"which day?" (hd)
  cut 2026-04-20
d_to: ?"which day?" (hd)
  cut 2026-04-20
